# Gitignored files a NEW worktree copies from the main checkout (.gitignore syntax; a
# file is copied only if it matches here AND git ignores it). Read by the Claude desktop
# app's worktree option and by the CLI worktree tool alike (2026-10-19).
#
# The fingerprint cache: keyed by the sim's own hash, so a stale copy is simply
# recomputed, and a fresh one spares the first `npm run build` the whole battery.
.sim-fingerprint.json
# The sfx order the soundboard saves, and the takes it names: "implement the sfx order"
# in a worktree needs both, and git carries neither.
docs/sfx-order.json
src/audio/sfx/incoming/**/*.wav
src/audio/sfx/incoming/**/*.mp3
src/audio/sfx/incoming/**/*.m4a
src/audio/sfx/incoming/**/*.ogg
#
# Deliberately NOT copied: node_modules (npm test and the build need none of it; only
# `cap sync` does, and a store build needs the generated android/ and ios/ projects,
# which only the main checkout has), android/key.properties
# (a signing key stays in one place), and the labs' saved state (the labs serve the main
# checkout, so a copy here would be read by nothing).
